"I'm approving PKT-0044. The diff does what the goal asks, keeps to the target and the budget, and doesn't break the contract.\n\n**Goal**\n- **Wrapper script:** `sdkjs-word.sh` plus `sdkjs-word-run.cjs` are written, and both are in `.theseus/oracle`, which the packet allows.\n- **Recorded results:** pass/fail, duration and skipped suites are recorded, including the reason for each skip.\n- **Card:** the oracle level and sources are set on the card.\n- **Suite list:** the runner reads the list of word suites and the skip list from upstream `runAll.js`, so it stays in step with upstream instead of copying the list by hand.\n\n**Scope and budget**\n- Six files changed and about 138 lines added. Only `atlas/sdkjs-word.md` was modified; the new files are under `.theseus/oracle`. The friction line and the spawn file are method files that rule R2 allows.\n\n**Contract**\n- No existing test or production code was touched.\n\n**TEP-0004 checks**\n- The Executor log is filled in.\n- The follow-up request is in `.theseus/spawn/`.\n- The surprising behavior is kept rather than hidden: `js-api-forms` fails because the `sdkjs-forms` add-on is missing, and that is now an explicit local skip with the error in its reason, plus the spawn file and a line on the card. The other two surprises (npm installing into the parent repo, and the suites needing network) are environment facts. They are handled in the script and written on the card.\n- Setting the level to `partial` is a reasonable, justified call.\n\n**Weaknesses that don't block approval**\n1. **The runner can pass with nothing run.** If upstream changes the layout of `runAll.js` so the pattern `^\\s*'(word/...html)',` finds nothing, or a filter matches no suite, it prints `0/0 suites passed` and exits 0. Wave-1 packets will use this oracle as their acceptance command, so a follow-up should make it fail when no suite runs (`todo.length === 0`), or when far fewer than the expected 41 suites are found.\n2. **The forms skip never 